From c497ebe12cf9b66583f4829af0b70eff255486db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:19:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/87] feat(tflite): POST /v1/images/classify served by
 tflite-server image models

Adds an image-classification deployment mode: ModelType::IMAGE_CLASSIFICATION,
the IImageClassificationServer capability, Router::classify_image and the
images/classify route under all four prefixes. The tflite backend detects a
text or image model directory, checks it against the model's type, confirms
the subprocess task over /health, and forwards raw image bytes as multipart
to tflite-server's /classify/image.

Image requests are capped before the body is read (411/413 from the
pre-routing handler), validated strictly (JPEG/PNG magic, strict base64,
16 MiB decoded), and never replayed after a backend crash: the backend is
reloaded and the client gets 502 backend_crashed_on_input. Backend 4xx
statuses nested under error.details now reach the client.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
